      "created_at": "2012-07-07T18:46:40.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Wait… they are TELLING people NOT to buy the game yet, and people are INSISTING that they buy 2 copies of it because they can’t wait to play it?</p>\n<p>… If that’s not an overwhelming success, then I don’t know what is.</p>\n<p>And no. Absolute Zero’s nemesis…</p>\n<p>is TEMPEST!</p>\n<p>(dun dun DUUNNNNNNNN)</p>\n<p>For real though, there’s nothing on AC that could possibly be anyone’s nemesis; especially not one for a completely different, non-aquatic hero.</p>\n<p>Unless the EE version of it has a different picture, I’ll gladly take that bet. It should be specified that we are betting that the thing on Correspondence IS or IS NOT his nemesis; “looks like” or “possibly could be” is not good enough. If, when the villain is revealed, it’s ambiguous or just hard to tell, we can ask Christopher.</p>\n<p>My bet is $30, to be delivered via the online purchase of a good or service of the winner’s choice. Nothing NSFW, illegal, or otherwise something you wouldn’t be willing to let everyone else in your family know you were buying, though.</p>",
